{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1983 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f8730f920128dc20942b77a6d141fdf490e9925d8e3dd34d432a0c9dc108b3e0" :edb/db-before-t 1982 :edb/db-after-t 1983 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535295 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:28:15.138Z" 13194139535295 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342315 13194139535295 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342322 13194139535295 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342308 13194139535295 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342319 13194139535295 true] [17592186101281 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535295 true] [17592186101281 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nWhat is the average value of $h(x) = \\sin 2x$ on the interval $[\\frac{π}{4}, \\frac{π}{2}]$?" 13194139535295 false] [17592186101281 1100 "What is the average value of $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ on the interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]?$" 13194139535295 true] [17592186101281 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }{(\\frac{1}{2})(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }(-1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342308 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342309 13194139535295 true] [17592186342308 1089 "q-15225" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342308 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535295 true] [17592186342308 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/6c70d5f15424c4d7d67a3998a785a214e46e8dfa47b83839fd99a574b2f756cf.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-1,6]$, is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(4,0)$ with radius $1.$ Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5].$" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342308 1113 #uuid "5ba1202f-23bb-59b7-8a58-51ad745d9aba" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342308 1145 "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-0}\\cdot (3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342310 13194139535295 true] [17592186342309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342311 13194139535295 true] [17592186342309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342312 13194139535295 true] [17592186342309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342313 13194139535295 true] [17592186342309 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342314 13194139535295 true] [17592186342309 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535295 true] [17592186342309 1041 "selection" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342309 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342310 13194139535295 true] [17592186342309 1110 #uuid "40a81efe-bb81-5712-8a60-556d0e16bd14" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342310 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342310 1111 #uuid "15c6edbe-0d21-5292-af54-3aee476000ec" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342311 1034 "5+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342311 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342311 1111 #uuid "93a81b6f-340c-5a38-93ca-46a5ff16f29a" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342312 1034 "3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342312 1111 #uuid "2383bcff-b9da-593f-88c2-e89a2f61299a" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342313 1034 "1+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342313 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342313 1111 #uuid "2ca59082-0a28-52be-80e6-2e8a54550b5a" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342314 1034 "1-\\frac{\\pi }{5}" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342314 1111 #uuid "8a29d6a2-873c-5695-b181-655cccae2a0c" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342315 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342316 13194139535295 true] [17592186342315 1089 "q-316302" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342315 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535295 true] [17592186342315 1100 "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342315 1113 #uuid "0b37cec7-6e6c-5351-8484-5f1e038f1fd6" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342315 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{8}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{8}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{9}}{9})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9\\pi }[(-1)^{9}-{1}^{9}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342316 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342317 13194139535295 true] [17592186342316 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342318 13194139535295 true] [17592186342316 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535295 true] [17592186342316 1041 "field-1" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342316 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342317 13194139535295 true] [17592186342316 1110 #uuid "08cc087a-9463-5e77-bef9-e6e9d28c2613" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342317 1034 "\\frac{2}{9\\pi}" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342317 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342317 1111 #uuid "15dbdf95-25d3-5705-9dda-b95d39ec2dda" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342318 1034 "0" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342318 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342318 1111 #uuid "9be1941e-5532-5a7a-8393-bb22b0656389" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342319 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342320 13194139535295 true] [17592186342319 1089 "q-344702" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342319 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535295 true] [17592186342319 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/8ddd8493662174e0ddaf9bdd63b0ec382f6bb25c9079f1a339b71400b8cf3860.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-6,6],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $15$, $60$ and $9,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-6,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342319 1113 #uuid "3f43cc69-bbf5-5e06-8e03-26d2b66ad73a" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342319 1145 "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-15+60-9=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-6)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342321 13194139535295 true] [17592186342320 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535295 true] [17592186342320 1041 "field-1" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342320 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342321 13194139535295 true] [17592186342320 1110 #uuid "0cdfcd64-e975-5f9a-a87e-656249c63b24" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342321 1034 "3" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342321 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342321 1111 #uuid "e6441432-c33b-55f9-8ad3-ece97b055c92" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342322 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342323 13194139535295 true] [17592186342322 1089 "q-74070" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342322 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535295 true] [17592186342322 1100 "Find $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=3-2x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $1.$" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342322 1113 #uuid "3eb6e7c8-042a-55b7-8ed7-70afc58e2b4b" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342322 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(3-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(3x-{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(3c-{c}^{2})-(0)] \\\\ 1 & =3-c \\\\ -2 & =-c \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342323 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342324 13194139535295 true] [17592186342323 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342325 13194139535295 true] [17592186342323 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342326 13194139535295 true] [17592186342323 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342327 13194139535295 true] [17592186342323 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342328 13194139535295 true] [17592186342323 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535295 true] [17592186342323 1041 "selection" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342323 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342326 13194139535295 true] [17592186342323 1110 #uuid "80f50ef6-6c7d-538f-b789-d3ce72a775a1" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342324 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342324 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342324 1111 #uuid "dad32c61-bf56-5ab6-ab8a-11cd7af4f4c9" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342325 1034 "3" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342325 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342325 1111 #uuid "2d95845d-452b-5660-b2df-86636bf6cb80" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342326 1034 "2" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342326 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535295 true] [17592186342326 1111 #uuid "ba37b375-a7f8-523a-bf42-0a38de161dae" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342327 1034 "1" 13194139535295 true] [17592186342327 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045